{
  "dom_id": "step-e10915",
  "name": "Example: Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- $(-3,1)\\cup(2,4)$\n\n- $[1,3)$\n\n- $(-\\infty, -2]$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-3,1) \\cup (2,4)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $-3,1,2,$ and $4.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open:\n\n- $[1,3)$ has two boundary points $1$ and $3,$ and the point $1$ lies in the set.\n\n- $(-\\infty,-2]$ has a boundary point $-2,$ which lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
